{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a set of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" files: reusable instructions that teach a model how\nto do one thing well (build a slide deck, follow your brand voice, fill a PDF).\nYou want the model to reach for the right one on its own, on whatever provider\nyou happen to run, without pasting every skill into the system prompt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-skills"},{"type":"text","value":" does this. It renders a short catalog of\nthe skills you offer, and gives the model a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" tool. The model reads\nthe catalog, picks a skill, calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":", and gets the full instructions\nback, only when it needs them. This works with any tool-calling model."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"portable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" path: it runs on the model you already use, no server\nsandbox required. For hosted skills that run in a provider's sandbox, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The two do not mix in one call,\nsee "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-skills#portable-vs-hosted-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable vs hosted"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/ai-skills","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-skills-to-a-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add skills to a chat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define a skill inline, then pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" array.\nThe middleware handles the catalog and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" tool for you."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: `\n# Building a deck\nUse python-pptx. Open or create the presentation, edit slides, then save.\nKeep one idea per slide.\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(pptx)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is the whole setup. The model now sees "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pptx-builder"},{"type":"text","value":" in its catalog and\ncan call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" to pull in the instructions when a deck-building task comes\nup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-model-sees","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the model sees"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" adds two things to the request:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A catalog in the system prompt, one line per skill (name plus description).\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" is constrained to your skill names, so the model\ncannot invent one."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" tool. When the model calls it, the middleware returns the\nskill body (frontmatter stripped) plus a list of any bundled resources."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loading the same skill twice in one conversation returns a short \"already\nloaded\" marker instead of repeating the body, so context stays lean."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"offer-more-than-one-skill","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Offer more than one skill"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an array. Skills are sorted by name and deduped for you."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: '# Building a deck\\nUse python-pptx. Edit slides, then save.',\n})\n\nconst brand = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'brand-voice',\n  description: 'Write in the company brand voice.',\n  instructions: '# Brand voice\\nWarm, direct, no jargon.',\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills([pptx, brand])],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline skills are the quickest start, but you rarely keep skills in code. Read\nthem from a folder, a build-time bundle, or your own database. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./skill-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill sources"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tune-the-catalog","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tune the catalog"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" takes options for the common cases:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"withSkills(sources, {\n  // Cap the catalog so a big skill library doesn't tax every request.\n  // Default 4000 tokens; throws if exceeded unless you supply a reducer.\n  maxCatalogTokens: 4000,\n\n  // Require a human approval before load_skill runs. Default false.\n  requireApproval: true,\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The catalog is rendered per model family: Anthropic models get the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<available_skills>"},{"type":"text","value":" XML they are tuned for, everything else gets a plain\nmarkdown list. You can override this with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderCatalog"},{"type":"text","value":" function or an\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructionTemplate"},{"type":"text","value":" string that has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{skills}"},{"type":"text","value":" placeholder."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-a-skill-s-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read a skill's files"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some skills bundle reference files (a style guide, a schema, an example). To let\nthe model read them, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createResourceTool"},{"type":"text","value":" to your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":"\nnotices it and tells the model it can call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"read_skill_resource"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { createResourceTool, inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-filler',\n  description: 'Fill a PDF form from a data object.',\n  instructions: '# Fill a PDF\\nSee references/fields.md for the field map.',\n  resources: { 'references/fields.md': 'name -> field_1\\nemail -> field_2' },\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [createResourceTool(pdf)],\n    middleware: [withSkills(pdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without the resource tool, resources are still listed in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":"\nresult, but the model is told they are not loadable in this setup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"skills-that-come-with-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skills that come with code"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some skills ship scripts, or their instructions say \"run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"python3 extract.py"},{"type":"text","value":"\".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" lists those scripts in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" result but does not run\nthem. Running code is your app's job, and you wire it up by passing your own\ntool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" composes with whatever tools you give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". So add an execution\ntool, and write the skill so it tells the model to call that tool. The skill\nsupplies the \"how\" (the command); your tool supplies the ability to run it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Your own execution tool. Run the command wherever you want: a provider\n// sandbox, a local isolate, a serverless worker. Guard it in production.\nconst executeShell = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'execute_shell',\n  description: 'Run a shell command and return its stdout.',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ command: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ stdout: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ command }) => {\n  const { stdout } = await runInYourSandbox(command)\n  return { stdout }\n})\n\nconst extractPdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-extract',\n  description: 'Extract text from a PDF with a small Python script.',\n  instructions: `\n# Extract PDF text\nRun this with the execute_shell tool, then return the text it prints:\n  python3 -c \"import sys, pypdf; ...\"\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [executeShell],\n    middleware: [withSkills(extractPdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Swap "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_shell"},{"type":"text","value":" for any tool: a container runner, a Code Mode sandbox, or\na remote worker. The skill never changes, only the tool behind it. For hosted\nskills that run in a provider's own sandbox instead, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./skill-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill sources"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — load skills from a folder, a build-time\nbundle, or your own store, and combine several sources."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./writing-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a skill source"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — back skills with S3, a database,\nor a registry, and prove it with the conformance suite."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — hosted skills that run in a\nprovider sandbox, and when to use them instead."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"install","text":"Install","level":2},{"id":"add-skills-to-a-chat","text":"Add skills to a chat","level":2},{"id":"what-the-model-sees","text":"What the model sees","level":2},{"id":"offer-more-than-one-skill","text":"Offer more than one skill","level":2},{"id":"tune-the-catalog","text":"Tune the catalog","level":2},{"id":"read-a-skill-s-files","text":"Read a skill's files","level":2},{"id":"skills-that-come-with-code","text":"Skills that come with code","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a set of `SKILL.md` files: reusable instructions that teach a model how\nto do one thing well (build a slide deck, follow your brand voice, fill a PDF).\nYou want the model to reach for the right one on its own, on whatever provider\nyou happen to run, without pasting every skill into the system prompt.\n\n`withSkills` from `@tanstack/ai-skills` does this. It renders a short catalog of\nthe skills you offer, and gives the model a `load_skill` tool. The model reads\nthe catalog, picks a skill, calls `load_skill`, and gets the full instructions\nback, only when it needs them. This works with any tool-calling model.\n\n> This is the **portable** path: it runs on the model you already use, no server\n> sandbox required. For hosted skills that run in a provider's sandbox, see\n> [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills). The two do not mix in one call,\n> see [Portable vs hosted](../tools/provider-skills#portable-vs-hosted-skills).\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/ai-skills\n```\n\n## Add skills to a chat\n\nDefine a skill inline, then pass it to `withSkills` in the `middleware` array.\nThe middleware handles the catalog and the `load_skill` tool for you.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: `\n# Building a deck\nUse python-pptx. Open or create the presentation, edit slides, then save.\nKeep one idea per slide.\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(pptx)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThat is the whole setup. The model now sees `pptx-builder` in its catalog and\ncan call `load_skill` to pull in the instructions when a deck-building task comes\nup.\n\n## What the model sees\n\n`withSkills` adds two things to the request:\n\n- A catalog in the system prompt, one line per skill (name plus description).\n  The `name` of `load_skill` is constrained to your skill names, so the model\n  cannot invent one.\n- A `load_skill` tool. When the model calls it, the middleware returns the\n  skill body (frontmatter stripped) plus a list of any bundled resources.\n\nLoading the same skill twice in one conversation returns a short \"already\nloaded\" marker instead of repeating the body, so context stays lean.\n\n## Offer more than one skill\n\nPass an array. Skills are sorted by name and deduped for you.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: '# Building a deck\\nUse python-pptx. Edit slides, then save.',\n})\n\nconst brand = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'brand-voice',\n  description: 'Write in the company brand voice.',\n  instructions: '# Brand voice\\nWarm, direct, no jargon.',\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills([pptx, brand])],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nInline skills are the quickest start, but you rarely keep skills in code. Read\nthem from a folder, a build-time bundle, or your own database. See\n[Skill sources](./skill-sources).\n\n## Tune the catalog\n\n`withSkills` takes options for the common cases:\n\n```ts ignore\nwithSkills(sources, {\n  // Cap the catalog so a big skill library doesn't tax every request.\n  // Default 4000 tokens; throws if exceeded unless you supply a reducer.\n  maxCatalogTokens: 4000,\n\n  // Require a human approval before load_skill runs. Default false.\n  requireApproval: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe catalog is rendered per model family: Anthropic models get the\n`<available_skills>` XML they are tuned for, everything else gets a plain\nmarkdown list. You can override this with a `renderCatalog` function or an\n`instructionTemplate` string that has a `{skills}` placeholder.\n\n## Read a skill's files\n\nSome skills bundle reference files (a style guide, a schema, an example). To let\nthe model read them, add `createResourceTool` to your `tools`. `withSkills`\nnotices it and tells the model it can call `read_skill_resource`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { createResourceTool, inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-filler',\n  description: 'Fill a PDF form from a data object.',\n  instructions: '# Fill a PDF\\nSee references/fields.md for the field map.',\n  resources: { 'references/fields.md': 'name -> field_1\\nemail -> field_2' },\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [createResourceTool(pdf)],\n    middleware: [withSkills(pdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nWithout the resource tool, resources are still listed in the `load_skill`\nresult, but the model is told they are not loadable in this setup.\n\n## Skills that come with code\n\nSome skills ship scripts, or their instructions say \"run `python3 extract.py`\".\n`withSkills` lists those scripts in the `load_skill` result but does not run\nthem. Running code is your app's job, and you wire it up by passing your own\ntool.\n\n`withSkills` composes with whatever tools you give `chat()`. So add an execution\ntool, and write the skill so it tells the model to call that tool. The skill\nsupplies the \"how\" (the command); your tool supplies the ability to run it.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Your own execution tool. Run the command wherever you want: a provider\n// sandbox, a local isolate, a serverless worker. Guard it in production.\nconst executeShell = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'execute_shell',\n  description: 'Run a shell command and return its stdout.',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ command: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ stdout: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ command }) => {\n  const { stdout } = await runInYourSandbox(command)\n  return { stdout }\n})\n\nconst extractPdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-extract',\n  description: 'Extract text from a PDF with a small Python script.',\n  instructions: `\n# Extract PDF text\nRun this with the execute_shell tool, then return the text it prints:\n  python3 -c \"import sys, pypdf; ...\"\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [executeShell],\n    middleware: [withSkills(extractPdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nSwap `execute_shell` for any tool: a container runner, a Code Mode sandbox, or\na remote worker. The skill never changes, only the tool behind it. For hosted\nskills that run in a provider's own sandbox instead, see\n[Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills).\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Skill sources](./skill-sources) — load skills from a folder, a build-time\n  bundle, or your own store, and combine several sources.\n- [Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) — back skills with S3, a database,\n  or a registry, and prove it with the conformance suite.\n- [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills) — hosted skills that run in a\n  provider sandbox, and when to use them instead.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Portable Agent Skills\nid: portable-agent-skills\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Give any tool-calling model a library of SKILL.md skills it can load on demand, on any provider, with the withSkills middleware from @tanstack/ai-skills.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - agent skills\n  - SKILL.md\n  - portable skills\n  - withSkills\n  - load_skill\n  - skill catalog\n---\n\nYou have a set of `SKILL.md` files: reusable instructions that teach a model how\nto do one thing well (build a slide deck, follow your brand voice, fill a PDF).\nYou want the model to reach for the right one on its own, on whatever provider\nyou happen to run, without pasting every skill into the system prompt.\n\n`withSkills` from `@tanstack/ai-skills` does this. It renders a short catalog of\nthe skills you offer, and gives the model a `load_skill` tool. The model reads\nthe catalog, picks a skill, calls `load_skill`, and gets the full instructions\nback, only when it needs them. This works with any tool-calling model.\n\n> This is the **portable** path: it runs on the model you already use, no server\n> sandbox required. For hosted skills that run in a provider's sandbox, see\n> [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills). The two do not mix in one call,\n> see [Portable vs hosted](../tools/provider-skills#portable-vs-hosted-skills).\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/ai-skills\n```\n\n## Add skills to a chat\n\nDefine a skill inline, then pass it to `withSkills` in the `middleware` array.\nThe middleware handles the catalog and the `load_skill` tool for you.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: `\n# Building a deck\nUse python-pptx. Open or create the presentation, edit slides, then save.\nKeep one idea per slide.\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(pptx)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThat is the whole setup. The model now sees `pptx-builder` in its catalog and\ncan call `load_skill` to pull in the instructions when a deck-building task comes\nup.\n\n## What the model sees\n\n`withSkills` adds two things to the request:\n\n- A catalog in the system prompt, one line per skill (name plus description).\n  The `name` of `load_skill` is constrained to your skill names, so the model\n  cannot invent one.\n- A `load_skill` tool. When the model calls it, the middleware returns the\n  skill body (frontmatter stripped) plus a list of any bundled resources.\n\nLoading the same skill twice in one conversation returns a short \"already\nloaded\" marker instead of repeating the body, so context stays lean.\n\n## Offer more than one skill\n\nPass an array. Skills are sorted by name and deduped for you.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pptx = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pptx-builder',\n  description: 'Build and edit PowerPoint decks with python-pptx.',\n  instructions: '# Building a deck\\nUse python-pptx. Edit slides, then save.',\n})\n\nconst brand = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'brand-voice',\n  description: 'Write in the company brand voice.',\n  instructions: '# Brand voice\\nWarm, direct, no jargon.',\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills([pptx, brand])],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nInline skills are the quickest start, but you rarely keep skills in code. Read\nthem from a folder, a build-time bundle, or your own database. See\n[Skill sources](./skill-sources).\n\n## Tune the catalog\n\n`withSkills` takes options for the common cases:\n\n```ts ignore\nwithSkills(sources, {\n  // Cap the catalog so a big skill library doesn't tax every request.\n  // Default 4000 tokens; throws if exceeded unless you supply a reducer.\n  maxCatalogTokens: 4000,\n\n  // Require a human approval before load_skill runs. Default false.\n  requireApproval: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe catalog is rendered per model family: Anthropic models get the\n`<available_skills>` XML they are tuned for, everything else gets a plain\nmarkdown list. You can override this with a `renderCatalog` function or an\n`instructionTemplate` string that has a `{skills}` placeholder.\n\n## Read a skill's files\n\nSome skills bundle reference files (a style guide, a schema, an example). To let\nthe model read them, add `createResourceTool` to your `tools`. `withSkills`\nnotices it and tells the model it can call `read_skill_resource`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { createResourceTool, inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\nconst pdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-filler',\n  description: 'Fill a PDF form from a data object.',\n  instructions: '# Fill a PDF\\nSee references/fields.md for the field map.',\n  resources: { 'references/fields.md': 'name -> field_1\\nemail -> field_2' },\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [createResourceTool(pdf)],\n    middleware: [withSkills(pdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nWithout the resource tool, resources are still listed in the `load_skill`\nresult, but the model is told they are not loadable in this setup.\n\n## Skills that come with code\n\nSome skills ship scripts, or their instructions say \"run `python3 extract.py`\".\n`withSkills` lists those scripts in the `load_skill` result but does not run\nthem. Running code is your app's job, and you wire it up by passing your own\ntool.\n\n`withSkills` composes with whatever tools you give `chat()`. So add an execution\ntool, and write the skill so it tells the model to call that tool. The skill\nsupplies the \"how\" (the command); your tool supplies the ability to run it.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { inlineSkill, withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\n// Your own execution tool. Run the command wherever you want: a provider\n// sandbox, a local isolate, a serverless worker. Guard it in production.\nconst executeShell = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'execute_shell',\n  description: 'Run a shell command and return its stdout.',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ command: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ stdout: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ command }) => {\n  const { stdout } = await runInYourSandbox(command)\n  return { stdout }\n})\n\nconst extractPdf = inlineSkill({\n  name: 'pdf-extract',\n  description: 'Extract text from a PDF with a small Python script.',\n  instructions: `\n# Extract PDF text\nRun this with the execute_shell tool, then return the text it prints:\n  python3 -c \"import sys, pypdf; ...\"\n`,\n})\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [executeShell],\n    middleware: [withSkills(extractPdf)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nSwap `execute_shell` for any tool: a container runner, a Code Mode sandbox, or\na remote worker. The skill never changes, only the tool behind it. For hosted\nskills that run in a provider's own sandbox instead, see\n[Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills).\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Skill sources](./skill-sources) — load skills from a folder, a build-time\n  bundle, or your own store, and combine several sources.\n- [Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) — back skills with S3, a database,\n  or a registry, and prove it with the conformance suite.\n- [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills) — hosted skills that run in a\n  provider sandbox, and when to use them instead.\n"}
